      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "707fed6a1ac7-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Direction: What will come in the place of the question mark &lsquo;?&rsquo; in the following question? 25% of 400 + 20% of 325 &ndash; 50% of 130 = ? 2",
      "questionHtml": "<p style=\"\"><strong>Direction:</strong> What will come in the place of the question mark &lsquo;?&rsquo; in the following question?</p>\n\n<p>25% of 400 + 20% of 325&nbsp;&ndash; 50% of 130 = ?<sup>2</sup></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "8",
          "html": "8"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "12",
          "html": "12"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "9",
          "html": "9"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "10",
          "html": "10"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Concept used:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Follow the <strong>BODMAS</strong> rule to solve this question, as per the order given below.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/10/image%20%284%29%20%281%29.png\" style=\"width: 440px; height: 247px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">25% of 400 + 20% of 325&nbsp;&ndash; 50% of 130 = ?<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; (25/100)&nbsp;&times; 400 + (20/100)&nbsp;&times; 325&nbsp;&ndash; (50/100)&nbsp;&times; 130 = ?<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 100 + 65&nbsp;&ndash; 65 = ?<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; ?<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= 100</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; ? = &radic;100</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; ? = 10</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&there4; Value of ? is 10</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/10/image%20%284%29%20%281%29.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "707fed6a1ac7-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "Find the value of y, \\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\% \\; \\times \\;12\\frac{1}{2}\\% \\; \\times \\;11\\frac{1}{9}\\% \\; \\times \\;y = \\;\\;4\\)",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Find the value of y,</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\% \\; \\times \\;12\\frac{1}{2}\\% \\; \\times \\;11\\frac{1}{9}\\% \\; \\times \\;y = \\;\\;4\\)</span></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "422",
          "html": "422"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "432",
          "html": "432"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "442",
          "html": "442"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "452",
          "html": "452"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><img height=\"31px\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/21/09/60b5d25a5006c24a9307e066_16306817747541.png\" width=\"147px\" />&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>We can solve percentage by remember some fraction</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\% = \\;\\frac{2}{3}\\)</span>,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\% = \\;\\frac{1}{8}\\)</span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(11\\frac{1}{9}\\% = \\;\\frac{1}{9}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;(2/3)&nbsp;&times; (1/8)&nbsp;&times; (1/9)&nbsp;&times; y = 4</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; y = (4&nbsp;&times; 3&nbsp;&times; 8 &times; 9)/2</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; y = 864/2</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; y = 432</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">&there4; The value of y is 432.</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Traditional method:</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\% \\; × \\;12\\frac{1}{2}\\% \\; × \\;11\\frac{1}{9}\\% \\; × \\;y = \\;\\;4\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n\n<p>According to the question, we have</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\% \\; × \\;12\\frac{1}{2}\\% \\; × \\;11\\frac{1}{9}\\% \\; × \\;y = \\;\\;4\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{200}}{3}\\% \\; × \\;\\frac{{25}}{2}\\% \\; × \\;\\frac{{100}}{9}\\% \\; × \\;y = \\;\\;4\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{200}}{300}\\ \\; × \\;\\frac{{25}}{200}\\ \\; × \\;\\frac{{100}}{900}\\ \\; × \\;y = \\;\\;4\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; (2/3)&nbsp;&times; (1/8)&nbsp;&times; (1/9)&nbsp;&times; y = 4</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; y = (4&nbsp;&times; 3&nbsp;&times; 8 &times; 9)/2</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; y = 864/2</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; y = 432</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The value of y is 432.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"F1_Harshit.S_09-06-21_Savita_D1.png\" src=\"https://chat.google.com/u/0/api/get_attachment_url?url_type=FIFE_URL&amp;content_type=image%2Fpng&amp;attachment_token=AAUuIGuhBy1E5lQTPZYP7SdKkTuyRgc4djqJbT8KcC98G5Oe18%2FsI%2BD3Ij83iuqEkjmOB9rm49NR%2BUJ2oIPBipMEcBP%2BELehSPkPTJYGqYnVtAnWCMJCcEe%2FMvXXe869wfBhKzRRAZcUFFO0Sy4ENss%2BI55iQTBeuE6VZG9YlCCeWGoVnVPxK3eZwAMYaBen21zZtsbH%2BiZFoW0HrN%2Fm%2BIUux2%2B678LWnUPZtCK4o1SearcGIukDDyd9JeCFMgXXA1sKMKIlbFYFDiv2JYQvDCpcWjKGUH1I5kX9ECpVn8e7l%2BSXo1dlFbPGnDi8bmsyOZTxAkZAXL63%2FE6rrY3rpLec%2BPWmOSqrJCN4QusgLGoli3QkGYto3c%2B7bWvr%2Fim8T8bQvf8Dz%2Bp7sGTc%2BwAwEIUlrIzMRWyjJ0w%2FXSIglf8Iu082pRGRQpUrFi7Ai5PjAe2yIDJ2NrNVc6uthIQiqODgzWgvZK5QfHy5kHYLYx4hJOvVcdUCv95vO9tCK8R6jvqcvvogialS47laGff5fFHp3Q%3D%3D&amp;sz=w512\" />&nbsp;</p>\n",
